# Keep Context Files In Sync

## Rule

Whenever a code change affects **Firebase read strategy**, **GitHub Actions strategy**, or **project structure/features**, you MUST also update the corresponding `.cursor/rules/` context file in the same task — not as a separate follow-up.

## Context files to update

| Pillar | Context file | Update when changing... |
|--------|-------------|------------------------|
| Firebase reads | `.cursor/rules/firebase-read-strategy.mdc` | Sync intervals, batch sizes, safety guards, read budget, DAU math, Room retention policy, any new Firebase read path |
| GitHub Actions | `.cursor/rules/github-actions-strategy.mdc` | Cron schedule, providers, API limits, dedup layers, metrics CSV columns, workflow steps, RSS feed count, secrets |
| General | `.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc` | Module boundaries, package names, key files, dependencies, conventions |

## When to trigger

- Adding/removing a news provider → update `github-actions-strategy.mdc`
- Changing sync parameters in `SyncManager.kt` → update `firebase-read-strategy.mdc`
- Changing Room deletion policy or adding/removing delete calls → update `firebase-read-strategy.mdc`
- Changing cron schedule or workflow steps → update `github-actions-strategy.mdc`
- Adding a new Firebase collection or read path → update `firebase-read-strategy.mdc`
- Changing DAU capacity or read budget math → update `firebase-read-strategy.mdc`
- Adding/removing RSS feeds → update `github-actions-strategy.mdc`
- Changing article quality filters → update `github-actions-strategy.mdc`
- Any structural change (new module, renamed package) → update `project-context.mdc`
- Adding/changing/removing dependencies → update `project-context.mdc`
- Adding/changing AdMob (ad units, placements, SDK config) → update `project-context.mdc`
- Adding new key files (components, screens, utilities) → update `project-context.mdc`

## How

Update the context file **values/tables/lists** to match the new code. Do not leave stale numbers or outdated parameters in context files.
